> The first of these allows you to hit monsters with scrolls and possibly
> invoke some of the scroll's magic, e.g. hitting monsters with a scroll of
> fire will burn them (effective against paper golems!).

Personally I like the patch but feel that the mechanic itself doesn't
make sense. Y'see, scroll magic is activated with a verbal component,
and the act of hitting with them constitutes a gestural ("somatic")
component. Also, I think it makes scroll identification (destroy armor,
fire etc.) undeservedly easier.

Now, if it had been hitting with _wands_...

(Also! The "roll" for scroll magic activation appears to be a Dex
check. Why dexterity? Must you hit with just the right part of the
scroll or something? And surely you should factor in your increase
accuracy rings as well?)



